{#- How a reference's skill name reaches the user on Mistral Vibe.

   The static references under `skills/` are copied verbatim into every target,
   so they name a sibling skill by its bare `/pipelex-<name>`, the spelling an
   agent resolves to `../pipelex-<name>/SKILL.md`. Vibe namespaces a plugin's
   skills and matches a typed name exactly, so a bare name handed to the user
   there is a command that resolves to nothing. This sentence, rendered on Vibe
   alone, has the agent rewrite the name as the user types it.

   Included at the head of the References section of the skills whose
   references route the user to another skill: run (`failed-run.md`,
   `by-id.md`), design (`stepwise.md`) and lab (`frame.md`). The size ceiling
   leaves scaffold and integrate no room for it, so the lines of their
   references that reach the user name the skill in words, the integrate skill
   or the run skill, and leave its spelling to the skill's own hand-offs. Every
   other reference names a sibling only to the agent, or in text written into
   the user's project, which keeps the bare spelling on purpose.

   Renders nothing on any other platform; on Vibe it ends with a blank line, so
   the list it precedes starts on its own line. -#}
{% if platform == "mistral-vibe" %}These references name a skill by its bare `/pipelex-<name>`; to the user, write it `{{ skill_prefix }}pipelex-<name>`, the only name {{ harness_name }} resolves.

{% endif %}
{#- -#}
